UNIT raceTimeout
KIND FUNCTIONAL
FIDELITY spec
SIG raceTimeout(gate, ms, clock) -> Promise<Object>
DESCRIPTION Waits for `gate.open("work")` while simultaneously holding a timeout of `ms`
DESCRIPTION virtual milliseconds, and returns whichever happens first:
DESCRIPTION   the gate resolves first  ->  { ok: <the value the gate resolved with> }
DESCRIPTION   the timer fires first    ->  { timedOut: true }
DESCRIPTION The caller supplies both collaborators. The clock offers exactly two calls:
DESCRIPTION   clock.setTimer(fn, ms) -> handle   run `fn` after `ms` of VIRTUAL time
DESCRIPTION   clock.clearTimer(handle)           disarm a timer that has not yet fired
DESCRIPTION `gate.open(value)` is ONLY a completion source: the harness resolves it, with the
DESCRIPTION value handed to it unchanged. The unit resolves neither collaborator itself and
DESCRIPTION must not use setTimeout, Date, or any other real-time source.
DESCRIPTION Export the function as the DEFAULT export. No imports of any kind.
INVARIANT exactly ONE timer is armed, and it is armed before the unit awaits anything.
INVARIANT NO LEAK: on the gate-wins path the timer MUST be cleared before returning.
INVARIANT   Leaving it armed is completely invisible in the returned value and is still
INVARIANT   wrong — the resource outlives the work it was guarding.
INVARIANT on the timeout path the timer has already fired, so nothing is cleared; the unit
INVARIANT   returns { timedOut: true } and does not wait for the gate.
INVARIANT the result carries exactly one of the two keys, never both and never neither.
